1177
01:47:30,393 --> 01:47:34,113
Minna-san! It's been 5 long years together, but we've done it!
Everyone! It's been 5 long years together, but we've done it!

1178
01:47:34,113 --> 01:47:36,933
We made it to year 5 together.

1179
01:47:37,353 --> 01:47:41,473
And while the future's looking pretty crazy and eventful,

1180
01:47:41,473 --> 01:47:46,293
let's take a little time to celebrate the story thus far, shall we?

1181
01:47:46,553 --> 01:47:53,713
And what better way to do that than with every Holo's bread-and-butter, the bane of every Deadbeat's wallet's existence?

1182
01:47:53,713 --> 01:47:55,613
That's right, everybody,

1183
01:47:55,613 --> 01:47:57,353
it's time for...

1184
01:47:57,573 --> 01:48:02,173
PREMIUM GOODS! Goods, goods, goods, goods!

1185
01:48:02,313 --> 01:48:05,033
Yeah, premium goods time, yeah.

1186
01:48:05,233 --> 01:48:10,373
You guys, you guys know what time it is. You get ready for it every year, right?

1187
01:48:10,373 --> 01:48:14,913
You guys know how I like to release merch that's more on the fashionable side than practical,

1188
01:48:14,913 --> 01:48:17,993
but I think there are a few things that you guys are going to love here.

1189
01:48:17,993 --> 01:48:23,833
And remember, if you grab it quick and manage to cop the premium limited set, you'll get a hand-signed postcard from me!

1190
01:48:23,833 --> 01:48:25,533
Pretty kawaii, happy!

1191
01:48:25,533 --> 01:48:28,193
But like always, supplies are extreme...

1192
01:50:00,712 --> 01:50:01,532
Ah, ah.

1193
01:50:02,372 --> 01:50:03,472
Hello.

1194
01:50:03,752 --> 01:50:08,932
Thank you so much everybody. I hope that you guys enjoyed the goods.
Thank you so much, everybody. I hope you guys enjoyed the goods.

1195
01:50:08,932 --> 01:50:12,212
Please look forward to receiving them. They're very cool.

1196
01:50:12,212 --> 01:50:15,932
I'm super excited with how they turned out.

1197
01:50:15,932 --> 01:50:20,532
Um so make sure that you don't miss it.

1198
01:50:20,532 --> 01:50:24,112
I think the shop will open about six minutes.
I think the shop will open in about six minutes.

1199
01:50:24,112 --> 01:50:29,332
You'll be able to pre-order your merch and get the limited if you're quick, you got to be quick,
You'll be able to pre-order your merch and get the limited... If you're quick, you gotta be quick,

1200
01:50:29,332 --> 01:50:32,312
cause they they do have a limited number.
'cause they do have a limited number.

1201
01:50:32,492 --> 01:50:36,172
Um, but yeah, please enjoy.

1202
01:50:36,172 --> 01:50:41,192
And thank you always for supporting me so much.

1203
01:50:41,192 --> 01:50:47,352
There will be a members-only encore after this featuring a few more songs and just getting to chat with my members,

1204
01:50:47,352 --> 01:50:49,472
which I'm excited about.

1205
01:50:49,672 --> 01:50:53,432
Um so please look forward to that.

1206
01:50:53,692 --> 01:50:54,772
And there's a new song.

1207
01:50:55,032 --> 01:50:58,652
I should look a little happier about that.

1208
01:50:58,652 --> 01:51:01,032
There's a new song coming out.

1209
01:51:01,432 --> 01:51:05,352
Um and I haven't really given any hints about what kind of song it is.

1210
01:51:05,352 --> 01:51:09,472
People are like, oh it's going to be so emotional.

1211
01:51:09,472 --> 01:51:14,752
This looks like an emotional song, but knowing what the song is makes me laugh really hard

1212
01:51:14,752 --> 01:51:17,732
cause it's actually a lot simpler than you think.

1213
01:51:17,932 --> 01:51:24,092
But something about my early music is that, man, I was so honest, you know?

1214
01:51:24,332 --> 01:51:33,632
And so I wanted to write a song that not just me myself, I as a person could relate to, but anyone, anyone who has an oshi could relate to.

1215
01:51:34,032 --> 01:51:46,972
And so I hope that you will enjoy it because it feels like an older Mori song while also being a newer Mori song is hard to explain, but I guess you'll just have to watch it and see.
And so I hope that you will enjoy it because it feels like an older Mori song while also being a newer Mori song—it's hard to explain, but I guess you'll just have to watch it and see.

1216
01:51:46,972 --> 01:51:50,412
MV's really cute, so we'll watch that premiere together too.

1217
01:51:50,412 --> 01:51:54,212
So don't go anywhere after the credits. Um please look forward to it.

1218
01:51:54,212 --> 01:51:56,932
New song, new songs stream it lots.
New song, new songs—stream it lots.

1219
01:51:57,132 --> 01:51:58,572
Stream it lots.

1220
01:52:05,812 --> 01:52:09,492
I'm staring at the ceiling, thinking

1221
01:52:09,492 --> 01:52:13,652
'Bout the way that time just slips away.

1222
01:52:13,872 --> 01:52:17,752
Another page is turning, but I

1223
01:52:17,752 --> 01:52:22,252
Wonder if we'll meet another day.

1224
01:52:22,612 --> 01:52:26,872
Even if the curtain falls...

1225
01:52:27,192 --> 01:52:31,792
Our story keeps on echoing through the halls.

1226
01:52:32,492 --> 01:52:37,692
Yeah, looking back, it's wild to see how far we've come.

1227
01:52:38,112 --> 01:52:42,892
A million memories and we're still not done.

1228
01:52:43,372 --> 01:52:47,732
Through every high and low, you stayed right by my side.

1229
01:52:48,052 --> 01:52:52,772
With you, I never had to run or hide.

1230
01:52:53,472 --> 01:52:57,612
So let the music play, let the rhythm take control.

1231
01:52:58,012 --> 01:53:02,752
You know you'll always have a piece of my soul.

1232
01:53:03,192 --> 01:53:07,772
Five years of magic, five years of grace.

1233
01:53:08,112 --> 01:53:12,792
Put a smile upon the reaper's face.

1234
01:53:13,472 --> 01:53:18,212
Ooh, ooh... Orpheus, sing to the night.

1235
01:53:18,612 --> 01:53:23,212
Guide us through the darkness with your light.

1236
01:53:23,832 --> 01:53:28,472
Ooh, ooh... till the end of the song.

1237
01:53:28,872 --> 01:53:33,692
With you is where I belong.

1238
01:53:42,872 --> 01:53:47,192
Looking at the stars above...

1239
01:53:47,552 --> 01:53:52,752
Sending you all my reaper love.

1240
01:53:53,232 --> 01:53:57,652
Whatever comes tomorrow, we'll face it hand in hand.

1241
01:53:58,012 --> 01:54:02,792
The best is yet to come across the land.

1242
01:54:03,352 --> 01:54:08,012
So thank you for everything, my dearest friends.

1243
01:54:08,372 --> 01:54:13,152
Our journey together never really ends.

1244
01:54:13,772 --> 01:54:18,252
Ooh, ooh... Orpheus, play on.

1245
01:54:18,652 --> 01:54:23,312
We'll keep on singing till the dawn.

1246
01:54:23,892 --> 01:54:28,532
Ooh, ooh... forever and a day.

1247
01:54:28,932 --> 01:54:35,692
Deadbeats, I'll never fade away.

1248
01:55:00,721 --> 01:55:01,741
watch it lots

1249
01:55:01,841 --> 01:55:04,741
and, um, share it around, I don't know, if you want, if you like it.

1250
01:55:04,941 --> 01:55:11,341
Um, but I still have one last song memory to replay in my mind here, in this beautiful area.

1251
01:55:11,601 --> 01:55:15,301
So, shall we run it? The last song of today?

1252
01:55:15,541 --> 01:55:17,261
Thank you so much, Deadbeats!

1253
01:55:17,641 --> 01:55:20,241
Catch you on the flipside. There might be an after party soon.
Catch you on the flip side. There might be an after party soon.

1254
01:55:20,241 --> 01:55:21,581
Let's go!

1255
01:55:26,871 --> 01:55:30,371
[Title: Orpheus Lyrics by Mori Calliope / Camellia Music by Camellia]

1256
01:55:32,533 --> 01:55:44,283
Ah...

1257
01:55:52,052 --> 01:56:00,682
Lost in thoughts, a frosted frame of mine, honest to god it's just not our time.

1258
01:56:00,982 --> 01:56:06,392
壊れかけた道の途中で / でも涙の後ろ隠せない
Broken halfway down the road, / but I can't hide the tears behind.

1259
01:56:06,812 --> 01:56:10,392
Coming of age for a stage that doesn't light up just right away.
Coming of age for a stage that doesn't light up right away.

1260
01:56:10,392 --> 01:56:16,402
They told us it might have - 「君へは、もう開かないから」
They told us it might have— "It'll never open up for you."

1261
01:56:17,292 --> 01:56:23,382
The cynic in my says, "Why'd you try? Why not give up and play the bad guy?"
The cynic in my head says, "Why'd you try? Why not give up and play the bad guy?"

1262
01:56:23,882 --> 01:56:27,652
We'll cut through the sounds...

1263
01:56:27,972 --> 01:56:35,292
望み絶ちたてながら / あなたの元すぐのなら / 崩れ落ちそうな身体
As my hopes shatter and fade, / if I could go straight to you— / my body feels like it's collapsing...

1264
01:56:35,742 --> 01:56:42,432
Darksome color, we choose to know...

1265
01:56:42,432 --> 01:56:49,442
The struggles of the sculpted page, we're living it, Crusader!

1266
01:56:49,442 --> 01:56:57,542
傷野郎だけど / この世の出口の / 水面は / 凪いでないぜえ
Even as a battered scoundrel, / the water's surface at this world's exit / isn't calm at all.

1267
01:56:57,842 --> 01:57:02,182
蜃気楼、出逢えたら
A mirage—if we could meet,

1268
01:57:02,362 --> 01:57:07,332
Can't find a reason to stay, some busted world bled us dry.

1269
01:57:07,332 --> 01:57:11,602
Left us just left to decay, we choose to go on anyway.

1270
01:57:15,542 --> 01:57:21,282
Uh-oh...

1271
01:57:21,462 --> 01:57:29,602
Lost in thoughts of a way-changing face, allies and friends hiding more than once face, not real surprising, wait, are you compromising?
Lost in thoughts of a way-changing face, allies and friends hiding more than one face, not real surprising, wait, are you compromising?

1272
01:57:29,992 --> 01:57:35,472
The sun is rising, and your horizon was friendships, acting like liz and the knives in your back, so what are you prioritizing?
The sun is rising, and your horizon was friendships, acting like lies and the knives in your back, so what are you prioritizing?

1273
01:57:35,782 --> 01:57:44,572
You weren't sick of crying, Seattle fire, but here we are, hanging on, fighting strongest spider.
You weren't sick of crying, Seattle fire, but here we are, hanging on, fighting, strong as a spider.

1274
01:57:42,542 --> 01:57:48,702
儚くて歩く力なら、もう閉じてしまいたい暗い夜空
If my strength to walk is fleeting, I'd rather just close my eyes in the dark night sky...

1275
01:57:48,882 --> 01:57:53,162
The cynic in my says, "Why'd you try? Why not give up and play the bad guy?"
The cynic in my head says, "Why'd you try? Why not give up and play the bad guy?"

1276
01:57:53,482 --> 01:58:07,492
What color and blinding light... 白黒まみれの街で / あなたのため息の影 / 私のかすがないで / 出したいだけ
What color and blinding light... In this black-and-white stained town, the shadow of your sigh— don't blur mine away, I just want to let it out!

1277
01:58:07,492 --> 01:58:16,192
We choose to know the struggles of the sculpted page, we're giving in though sunny...

1278
01:58:16,512 --> 01:58:24,452
夜空だって / 美味しくねえ、果てしない / 世界を駆けて行こう
Even if the night sky / isn't sweet, let's run across this endless world!

1279
01:58:24,452 --> 01:58:32,332
Can't find a reason to stay, some busted world bled us dry. 出会えた奇跡なら 二人なら
Can't find a reason to stay, some busted world bled us dry. The miracle of meeting you, if it's the two of us...

1280
01:58:32,332 --> 01:58:38,592
Lost in thoughts of a way-changing face, allies and friends hiding more than one space.

1281
01:58:38,742 --> 01:58:45,682
The sun is rising, and your horizon was friendship, but like... The lights and sights and sounds are treasures.

1282
01:58:54,312 --> 01:59:07,212
こんない世界に / 昂がって歩く / 力なんてないんだ
In a world like this, / I don't have the strength to get worked up / and walk anymore.

1283
01:59:09,682 --> 01:59:21,432
Face of this world can kill the inner spark, why don't we turn the scuffed up page, we're riding in, common up!
Face of this world can kill the inner spark, why don't we turn the scuffed-up page, we're riding in, common up!

1284
01:59:21,432 --> 01:59:28,132
世界中じゃ / 微笑みだけじゃなくて / 君の夜明けは / 滅多にフェアじゃないぜ
All over the world, / it's not just smiles— / your dawn / is rarely ever fair.

1285
01:59:28,282 --> 01:59:36,532
It's your life! 儚くて歩く力なら、もう閉じてしまいたい暗い夜空
It's your life! If my strength to walk is fleeting, I'd rather just close my eyes in the dark night sky...

1286
01:59:39,482 --> 01:59:47,752
Tomorrow's a brand new day! Like all those optimists say, "Fuck the truth, as ruthless as it might be, rain..."

1287
01:59:47,752 --> 01:59:53,292
The question is: will your battle pay? What's your breeze on the stage?

1288
01:59:53,292 --> 02:00:01,742
This shining world, let us stray, won't lead us on to decay. I choose to love it anyway!

1289
02:00:06,667 --> 02:00:12,507
Wait, do you still know

1290
02:00:12,507 --> 02:00:16,887
the strokes of the scaffold?

1291
02:00:16,887 --> 02:00:20,447
A page we live in...

1292
02:01:50,272 --> 02:01:59,532
...and you DEAD BEATS!!

1293
02:02:00,272 --> 02:02:09,832
Happy 5 years.

1294
02:02:12,612 --> 02:02:32,052
Here's to more.

1295
02:02:34,342 --> 02:02:37,602
What are you still doing here? The show's over.

1296
02:02:37,822 --> 02:02:41,422
Go watch the music video!

1297
02:02:41,422 --> 02:02:42,982
Bye!

1298
02:02:43,386 --> 02:03:14,572
[Text: Thank You all for 5 incredibly Strange, wonderful, whimsical at times painful but so, so special Years as your Mori. There are so many more views I want to see, but for now, just to know how thankful I am that I get to be your Pink woman. Always. We laughed. We cried. We cringed. And we'll do it again, dammit!! ...and you DEAD BEATS!! Happy 5 years. Here's to more.]

